 plus a bare-domain link fix (todotxt.org -> https://todotxt.org); docs/DECISIONS.md had 2 links one directory level off (./specifications/process.md and ./ontology/README.md should have been ../, since the file lives in docs/) -- fixed.$ !5 ^2026-09-21T20:32 #01a0c72b-c463-7709-8e34-1e31df7ef245
[ ] Add a lint for decision text inside an action description $Follow-up from the single-source knowledge rule (support 01a0b5d0-da38), found 2026-09-22. The rule now says decisions live only in DECISIONS.md and actions link to them, but nothing enforces it: a decision heading pasted into an action description is still invisible. Add a lint that flags it. Decided scope when the rule was written: a narrow rule, not a broad prose detector. Match a genuine decision heading only -- a markdown heading or a Decision <n>: label inside the description -- NOT the legitimate inline citations the repo already uses (DECIDED 2026-09-18, Decision 41, RESOLVED ...), which are links and task history, not duplicated decision text. Verified 2026-09-22 that no existing .actions file matches the narrow pattern, so the rule ships quiet. Deferred rather than done with the rule because it needs a new lint code, which means documenting it in specifications/linting.md and clearhead.nvim doc/clearhead.txt in the same commit, plus a false-positive review of historical action notes. Touch points: clearhead-core/src/workspace/actions/lint.rs (a new check beside check_excessive_duration), the lint code registry in specifications/linting.md, and the diagnostic list in clearhead.nvim doc/clearhead.txt.$ !4 ^2026-09-22T12:59 #01a0cab3-ea83-7980-9b89-80bf3f92b90e
